WEBVTT

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:18.880
This giant puzzle moves every time I retrieve
a missing Number Card.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:24.630
There are 99 cards, the same
number of memories I’m missing.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.050
Is this structure
some kind of message?

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.760
Why is this inside Yuma’s key?

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:38.970
Did someone anticipate
that I would lose my memories?

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.680
Oh no!

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.190
I’m going to be late!

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:57.700
Watch outl! Didn’t
you see the light-

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:01.450
You’re Shark!

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:15.020
Where’s Shark going?

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.160
I made it in time.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.120
Yuma.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.630
Show me your deck.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:27.400
Hey!

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.760
Huh?

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:32.610
It’s not here.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:33.820
What isn’t?

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:36.350
Numbers.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:37.780
Where are those cards?

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:41.540
They’re only in my deck
when he’s around.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:42.490
He?

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:44.250
Astral!

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.210
The duel ghost.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:48.670
What are you talking about?

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:55.380
To summarize, Yuma is a bad duelist right now
because he doesn’t have a Number Card.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.480
That’s not
a nice thing to say.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:03.300
You make it sound like I only won
because of the Numbers and him!

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.850
Because that’s true.

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:10.060
To summarize, Yuma couldn’t have beat Shark
or Tokunosuke without them.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:13.900
You don’t know how
awesome my kattobing is!

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.860
My duel sphinx
is now a lot better!

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:19.940
Sphinx?

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:22.240
He meant to say tactics.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.560
Wow!

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:26.080
Tetsuo, you’re Yuma’s translator!

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:31.040
Yuma, can you prove that you’re
strong even without a Number?

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.780
I can!

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:38.300
I’m going to duel Shark again
and beat him without using a Number Card!

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:39.670
Yuma?

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:40.800
You...

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.320
I see.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.530
That will confirm your skills.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:46.880
All right!

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.520
I’m going to meet
Shark right away!

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:50.340
Wait, Yuma.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:53.230
I heard that he’s
been skipping school.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:58.990
It’s because Shark’s status plummeted
when he lost his duel against you.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:03.420
Rumors say that he’s hanging out
with a bad crowd.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.690
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.800
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:17.860
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:21.970
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:29.350
In truth, I was sad
until I met you

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:35.990
I lied, thinking it was
easier to be alone

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:42.450
Even though we don’t like
the same books or hobbies

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:46.330
You’re the only one
who agreed with me

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:49.450
Joy and sadness and anger
and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:51.420
There’s no harmony and scenario
without differences

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.540
Everyone is not the same

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:59.550
That’s the reason for living

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:04.800
Even if the sounds
are dissonant at times

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:10.220
That’s why I never give up
I believe my strength will get me through

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:14.220
I travel to
the edge of the world

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:17.940
The sights I see
with you are the truth

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.780
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:24.320
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:27.410
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:31.540
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:41.210
\hShark’s Counterattack!\h

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:41.210
Number 10:

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:37.370
Welcome.

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:41.210
Thank you for shopping with us today.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.930
They don’t understand.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.950
I’m much stronger than before.

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:50.930
Where are you going, Yuma?

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.810
Why are you showing up now?

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.820
It’s your fault
that I’m in a pickle!

00:04:57.820 --> 00:04:58.730
What do you mean?

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.110
I’m going to duel Shark again.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:02.790
Shark?

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:05.660
The boy who used the Number?

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.710
Why do you
have to duel him?

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:09.280
It’s none of your business!

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:11.620
You have nothing to do
with this duel!

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.640
In fact, I can’t
have you involved.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.080
Wait!

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:20.040
Yuma, you’re really going?

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:22.050
Of course!

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:25.310
If I don’t meet Shark,
I can’t duel him.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:33.060
Shark is here.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:36.030
This place is dangerous!

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:37.270
Hey, Yuma!

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.910
What a strange place.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:49.910
Yuma!

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:50.780
Hey!

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:53.380
Let’s go home!

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:55.330
This place is...

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.730
Tetsuo!

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:02.510
What do you rugrats want?

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:05.210
This is our territory.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:06.840
Let him go!

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:09.970
Yuma!

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:12.010
Let me go!

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:15.310
This kid is energetic.

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:20.920
Rikuo and Kaio,
who are these guys?

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:25.540
I’ll take you on,
so let me go!

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:27.050
You shouldn’t try.

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:29.470
It’s obvious that there’s
a physical size difference.

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:30.880
Back off!

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:33.060
Bro, what should
we do with them?

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:34.880
Let’s beat them up.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:36.330
Stop.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.910
Let them go.

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:42.630
Shark...

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:45.710
You know them?

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:46.610
Yeah.

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:48.970
It’s your lucky day.

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:00.480
You shouldn’t have come here.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.170
Wait, Shark!

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:04.200
I came to see you!

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:05.680
Me?

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:08.070
Duel me again!

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.890
That’s impossible.

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:14.040
Why?

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:16.100
I quit dueling.

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:20.920
I don’t plan
to duel ever again.

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:28.420
Shark has fallen off.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:31.870
Those brothers are notorious duelists.

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:35.880
They appear in tournaments
and extort people.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:37.390
What’s wrong, Yuma?

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:40.150
Yuma...

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:43.100
Why did he quit dueling?

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:46.440
Yeah.

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:49.620
Why did he quit dueling?

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.270
Because he lost against you.

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:54.910
Why would he quit dueling
because he lost against me?

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:58.690
You lose something by losing.

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:01.810
Lose by losing?

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:11.620
Come to think of it, I heard that Shark began to stray
after appearing in the national duel tournament.

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:14.780
Something may have happened then.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:19.410
He...

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:23.650
He was supposed to love dueling.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:32.450
Where’s Yuma?

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.510
He left in a hurry.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:36.700
Is Yuma planning to...

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:38.780
What do you want?

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:40.780
Duel me!

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:43.560
What’s so fun hanging out
with those thugs?

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:45.590
You don’t understand.

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:48.040
You can understand everything
about your opponent by dueling!

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:50.000
Right?

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:52.420
Now duel me!

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:54.480
I quit dueling!

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:56.260
Stop bothering me!

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.490
Shark, wait!

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:07.400
I’m kattobing!

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:16.180
I’m kattobing!

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:24.750
He finally gave up.

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:26.710
Shark!

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:30.630
Duel me...

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:34.750
Why did you give up dueling?

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:38.890
What’s wrong with you?

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:42.040
Why are you
making such a fuss?

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:45.060
Because we’re friends, of course!

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:49.900
Once you duel someone,
he’s no longer a stranger. He’s a friend!

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:53.010
I know you feel the same!

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:56.270
Are you serious?

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:57.310
I’m serious!

00:09:57.310 --> 00:10:00.970
If I win, you have to
leave the thugs!

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:04.180
What will you bet?

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:05.080
I’ll...

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.750
...wager this!

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:09.780
Yuma, that’s...

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:11.480
You stay quiet!

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:14.060
Interesting.

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:16.260
I hope you don’t regret it.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:19.930
You’re going to lose your
most valuable item this time.

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:31.360
Yuma, are you really doing this?

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:35.310
I said this duel
has nothing to do with you!

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:38.030
I’m not going to use
a Number in this duel.

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:39.410
What do you mean?

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:42.600
Only a Number can
destroy a Number.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:45.370
But Shark no longer
has a Number.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:46.920
Yuma...

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:51.790
I won’t use a Number against someone
who doesn’t have one because it’s not fair!

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:57.400
And my skills have greatly
improved than before.

00:10:57.400 --> 00:11:00.790
I’ll show that I can win
without your help!

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:03.630
Understood. I’ll just watch.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:07.850
I haven’t forgotten
that I lost against you.

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:18.650
Maybe I’ve been waiting
for this moment!

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:20.280
Here I go!

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:22.950
Duel Disk set!

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.330
D-Gazer set!

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:33.830
AR Vision Link complete.

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:35.780
Duel!

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:39.470
Duel!

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:43.590
Here I go!

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:45.760
My turn! I draw!

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:48.220
I summon Gogogo Golem!

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:53.350
Be careful, Yuma.

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:55.780
He uses powerful monsters.

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:57.320
Gogogo Golem won’t be enough to-

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.320
I know!

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:00.820
I set one card!

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:04.490
The first player can’t
attack on the first turn.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:05.530
I end my turn.

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:09.250
My set card is Battle Break.

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:14.690
When he attacks, this trap destroys
his monster and ends the battle.

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:18.230
Now he can’t attack so easily.

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:20.260
My turn! I draw!

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:23.380
I summon Friller Rabca!

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:29.740
Friller Rabca has 700 ATK.

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:31.180
What is he planning?

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:35.190
Then I Special Summon Shark Stickers!

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:44.250
When a Fish-Type monster is successfully summoned,
I can Special Summon Shark Stickers from my hand!

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:46.240
Two Level 3 monsters!

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:47.530
Can it be?

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:52.110
I overlay Level 3 Friller Rabca
and Shark Stickers!

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:58.220
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:12:58.220 --> 00:12:59.710
Xyz Summon!

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:03.670
Come, Submersible Carrier Aero Shark!

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:09.610
1900 ATK!

00:13:09.610 --> 00:13:12.000
That’s stronger than Gogogo Golem!

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:15.810
But my trap card will
stop Shark’s attack.

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:19.280
I activate Aero Shark’s effect!

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:22.860
Once per turn,
by using one Overlay Unit...

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:27.240
...you take 400 points of damage
for every card in my hand!

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:30.070
I have four
cards in my hand.

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:33.200
Therefore, you take
1600 points of damage.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:34.250
What?

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:50.470
I activate the Quick-Play Spell
Mystical Space Typhoon from my hand!

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:54.890
Mystical Space Typhoon destroys one spell
or trap card on the field.

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:58.520
My trap!

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:01.080
Go, Aero Shark!

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:02.480
Attack Gogogo Golem!

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:04.650
Big Eater!

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:11.370
I set one card
and end my turn.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:18.540
Wow! Yuma is down
to 2300 LP in one turn!

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:21.410
Shark is incredibly powerful.

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:22.250
Yuma...

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.080
Now what?

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:25.960
Aren’t you here to defeat me?

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:31.040
You want to defeat me when I’m down
so that you can laugh at me again!

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:31.890
You’re wrong!

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:35.020
That’s not why I’m here.

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:39.410
I’ll lose without doing anything.

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:41.040
If only I could use
a Number...

00:14:41.470 --> 00:14:42.520
Damn!

00:14:43.090 --> 00:14:44.730
My turn! I draw!

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:48.490
This is...

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:50.980
I summon Gagaga Magician!

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:59.290
Once per turn, Gagaga Magician can change its Level
to a number between 1 and 8.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:02.710
And I have Monster
Reborn in my hand.

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:09.160
If I use this to resurrect Gogogo Golem,
I can summon Utopia to the field!

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:13.980
I said that I wouldn’t use
a Number during this duel.

00:15:14.650 --> 00:15:15.880
But...

00:15:15.880 --> 00:15:18.880
Bring out your Number!

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:20.230
It’s your trump card!

00:15:21.510 --> 00:15:24.230
What is Shark talking about?

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:26.710
Only a Number can
destroy a Number.

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:29.280
He knows that!

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:32.000
Now bring out your Number!

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:35.120
Do you think you can win
without using that card?

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:42.460
It’s only worth winning this duel
if I defeat you while you’re using a Number!

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:46.140
Shark is incredibly powerful.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.660
At this rate, I’ll...

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:52.680
In order to defeat Shark...

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:53.580
Yuma.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:56.140
You’re planning to use a Number?

00:15:57.300 --> 00:16:03.140
You said that using a Number
during this duel would be cheating.

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:05.440
But I won’t stop you.

00:16:05.870 --> 00:16:08.400
I don’t want to lose
the King’s Key.

00:16:10.340 --> 00:16:14.110
Use a Number
if it will help you win!

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:16.850
That’s right!

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:20.080
This duel isn’t about my pride!

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.830
I have to save Shark!

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:28.750
I activate the spell
card Monster Reborn!

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:32.440
I resurrect Gogogo Golem
from my graveyard!

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:38.170
I overlay Level 4 Gagaga Magician
and Gogogo Golem!

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:45.040
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:47.650
Xyz Summon!

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:50.890
Appear, Number 39!

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.320
Utopia!

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:02.770
Yuma used a Number?

00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:06.040
He promised
that he wouldn’t use it!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:10.810
To summarize, Yuma’s
dueling relies on Numbers.

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:13.170
The Number appeared.

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:15.180
I’m getting fired up!

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:17.970
Go, Utopia!

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:20.060
Attack Aero Shark!

00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:22.180
Not good enough!

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:25.220
I activate Friller Rabca’s effect!

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:28.860
By banishing Friller Rabca
from my graveyard...

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:35.230
...your monster’s attack is negated,
and it loses 500 ATK.

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:37.490
What?

00:17:37.850 --> 00:17:40.250
I activate the trap Fish Rain!

00:17:40.250 --> 00:17:43.470
When a Fish-Type monster is banished...

00:17:43.470 --> 00:17:47.210
I can Special Summon a Level 3-or-below
Fish-Type monster from my hand.

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:51.140
I summon Big Jaws!

00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:59.210
No way...

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:01.890
Even Utopia couldn’t destroy Aero Shark!

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:05.020
You made a playing mistake
because you tried to win quickly.

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:10.230
Monster Reborn can also resurrect a monster
from the opponent’s graveyard.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:14.380
If you resurrected Friller Rabca
from Shark’s graveyard...

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:18.870
...you could’ve used Gagaga Magician’s effect
to Xyz Summon Leviathan Dragon.

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:22.160
Friller Rabca’s effect wouldn’t have activated.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:26.970
And you could’ve used Leviathan
Dragon’s effect to destroy Aero Shark.

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:30.330
Be quiet! I’m still fine!

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:32.310
Utopia has 2000 ATK.

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:37.590
Shark doesn’t have a monster on his field
with more ATK than Utopia.

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:40.010
I end my turn!

00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:42.760
My turn! I draw!

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:45.940
I activate Aero Shark’s effect!

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:49.060
Once per turn,
by using one Overlay Unit...

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:54.480
...you take 400 points of damage
for every card in my hand!

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:56.280
I have two
cards in my hand.

00:18:56.910 --> 00:19:00.650
Therefore, you take
800 points of damage!

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:04.960
Then I summon Skull Kraken!

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:09.120
Two Level 3 monsters!

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:10.830
Don’t get flustered.

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:14.090
He doesn’t have a card
that can destroy a Number.

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:19.300
I overlay Level 3 Skull
Kraken and Big Jaws!

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:23.230
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:19:23.230 --> 00:19:24.810
Xyz Summon!

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:28.390
Appear, Black Ray Lancer!

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.860
This duel is mine.

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:40.530
I activate Black Ray Lancer’s effect!

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:46.300
By using one Overlay Unit,
your monster’s effects are negated this turn!

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:47.330
What?

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:53.340
Utopia!

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:58.840
A Number’s invincibility is an effect!

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:01.990
If that effect is gone,
it can be destroyed!

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:07.720
No way... Utopia’s
Number effect is negated!

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:10.020
Go, Black Ray Lancer!

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:12.520
Black Spear!

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:18.890
Utopia!

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:23.700
Utopia was destroyed.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:26.700
He knows the Number’s weak point.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:29.410
Aero Shark attacks you directly!

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:31.860
Big Eater!

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:45.580
To summarize, he totally lost.

00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:47.470
Yuma lost.

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:50.230
This must be a joke.

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:52.230
I used a Number,
but I still lost.

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:55.780
You’re too weak.

00:20:55.780 --> 00:21:01.150
I can’t believe losing to such a
horrible duelist made me lose my way.

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:03.310
It makes me laugh!

00:21:05.170 --> 00:21:08.280
As promised, I’ll take this.

00:21:10.110 --> 00:21:13.710
Because we’re friends, of course!

00:21:21.790 --> 00:21:24.800
This isn’t even worth destroying.

00:21:29.060 --> 00:21:30.260
Shark...

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.790
Wait!

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:34.860
Yuma, you don’t understand.

00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:36.980
I’m hanging out with them
because I want to.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:43.650
They gave me a home
when I lost mine.

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:45.820
Don’t bother me again!

00:21:47.190 --> 00:21:48.590
Shark...

00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:51.430
Yuma...

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:15.380
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:15.380 --> 00:22:17.380
This week’s quiz:

00:22:17.380 --> 00:22:20.950
Which spell card can you activate
during your opponent’s turn?

00:22:20.950 --> 00:22:24.480
An Equip Spell
or a Quick-Play Spell?

00:22:30.400 --> 00:22:35.000
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:39.870
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:54.600
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.600 --> 00:22:59.480
Average scores in science
and social studies I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:02.480
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:04.770
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.770 --> 00:23:07.190
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:08.820
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:13.760
Let’s say I wrote
the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.760 --> 00:23:18.040
Will that change the future a year
or a decade from now?

00:23:18.600 --> 00:23:23.700
The world I drew
at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.700 --> 00:23:28.720
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:33.220
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:37.270
Nothing is correct!

00:23:40.960 --> 00:23:44.940
He’s a fool, but
he was never a liar!

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:47.400
You’re not acting like yourself.

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:48.780
Stop already, Yuma!

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:50.160
Why are you doing
this for Shark?

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:51.580
No!

00:23:51.580 --> 00:23:55.580
This duel is also for me
because I lied!

00:23:55.580 --> 00:23:57.080
You’re so annoying!

00:23:57.080 --> 00:23:58.750
Why are you
making such a fuss?

00:23:58.750 --> 00:24:00.960
Because we’re friends, of course!

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:09.970
\h\hYuma and Shark: An Injury-Filled Tag Duel\h\h

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:06.940
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Yuma and Shark: An Injury-Filled Tag Duel”

00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:08.470
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.870 --> 00:24:14.950
The answer is... a Quick-Play Spell!

00:24:14.950 --> 00:24:19.690
You can usually only activate
spell cards during your turn.

00:24:19.690 --> 00:24:22.980
But you can use Quick-Play Spells
even during your opponent’s turn.
